course: dictionary
lesson: 15927
title: Unreached: not yet got to
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unreached means not yet reached or got to. Look at its parts: un- means not, and reached means got to. So an unreached place is one that nobody has got to yet. «The explorers wanted to reach the valley, but it was still unreached.»
explain: The word can also be about people. «Some older people were still unreached by the new phone service.» Here it means those people had not yet been contacted or helped. Look at the words around it: new service, still, and not yet. These are the clues.
explain: In maths, an unreached target means the total is still below the target. «The class needed 60 cans but had only 45, so their target was unreached.» The clue is the word target: the number has not yet got up to it.
fact: Unreached means not yet reached or got to.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unreached means not reached.
fact: For people, unreached means not yet contacted or helped.
fact: In maths, a target is unreached when the total is still below it.
fact: Unreached is a rare word, so it is good to notice how the words around it give its meaning.
exercise: «The explorers wanted to find the unreached valley beyond the mountains.» What does unreached mean here? | Very cold and icy | Already explored many times | *Not yet reached or got to | Lost forever in the snow
exercise: «The class collected 45 cans, but their target was 60, so the target was still unreached.» Why is the target unreached? | The total is above the target | The cans were all lost | The class has finished the task | *The total is still below the target
exercise: «Some older people were still unreached by the new phone service.» Find and copy the one word that means not yet reached. | phone | older | *unreached | service
test: «The nurse visited every house, but one family was still unreached.» What does unreached mean for people here? | Angry at the nurse | *Not yet contacted or helped | Cured of all illness | Moved to a new house
test: Un- means not in unreached. Which word also uses un- to mean not? | reaching | ready | *unhappy | reached
exam: «The map showed one unreached village high in the hills.» What does unreached mean? | Closed for the winter | Full of people | Found and drawn on the map | *Not yet reached or got to
